  "query_preview": "..\nDaytime heating warranted thunderstorms and heavy downpours over \nnorthern Guam earlier this afternoon. As a col continues to move over\nthe region from the northeast, winds will remain light and variable \nat least until the weekend. Therefore, island-effect showers and \nthunderstorms are to be expected for the next couple of afternoon \nperiods followed by isolated showers in the overnight hours. A \nfairly dry environment with light to gentle easterly trade winds is \npossible starting early next week. Due to the increase in wind speed,\nisland-effect showers, if any, may be concentrated over western \ncoastal waters at least until next weekend. There is high uncertainty\nregarding a late-week approach of Invest 93W, so isolated \nthunderstorms are included in the last few periods of the forecast.",
